.TH "AG\-CLI\-REPO\-FORK" "1" "2026\-10\-09" "AtomGit CLI 0.7.4" "AtomGit CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
\&ag\-cli\-repo\-fork \- Fork a repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&ag\-cli repo fork [<owner>/<repo>] [flags]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Fork a repository on AtomGit.
.PP
\&Creates a fork of the specified repository under your account or an organization.
.PP
\&By default, the fork will have the same visibility as the original repository.
\&Use \-\-private or \-\-public to override.
.PP
\&When OWNER/REPO is omitted, the repository is inferred from the current Git repository. An explicit OWNER/REPO argument always takes precedence. Remote selection prefers remote.pushDefault, the current branch upstream, origin, then a unique AtomGit/GitCode remote.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-clone\fR
\&Clone the forked repository
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-description <string>\fR
\&Description for the forked repository
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-name <string>\fR
\&Name for the forked repository
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-private\fR
\&Make the forked repository private
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
\&Make the forked repository public
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH INHERITED OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
\&Show help for command
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
\&Disable terminal output sanitization for machine processing
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
